Telegraf: general/get, output/get, service/status; model output flags include
InfluxDB v1/v2, Graphite and Prometheus. Only selected public fields leave the
parser. HTTP(S) metrics URLs omit user info, query and fragment components.

CrowdSec: alerts/search and decisions/search. Retain the first50 records and
upstream totals separately. Partial/inconsistent pages and invalid identities
are unavailable. The UI explicitly identifies truncated windows.

NetFlow: diagnostics/netflow/getconfig and diagnostics/netflow/status.
Configuration uses selected interface/version options and collect.enable.
Enabled configuration requires both a target and selected interface; active
runtime is reported independently. Egress interface scope is retained.

Squid: forward.port, general.cache.local.enabled, and individual access/store
logging flags. Monit service/alert booleans are normalized and every searched
inventory must be complete. Tailscale reports only selected exit-node options.

Unknown service values are unavailable, not stopped. Only running/stopped/
disabled and NetFlow active/inactive are interpreted as known runtime states.
Required read errors propagate safely; cancellation is never an empty success.

Tests use the actual OPNsense HTTP client with synthetic responses, plus real
PostgreSQL/ASGI and real UI components. They do not qualify installed firmware,
normal authenticated device operations, service health, throughput, hardware
writes, restoration, host-loss HA, production RTO/RPO or enterprise readiness.
Older firmware/plugin schemas that omit required fields are refused, not
silently guessed. Validate your exact versions before production operation.
